# Toolchain pins, read by CI and tests/stunt_lib.sh. Evidence-based, as in the
# rest of the Aether family: AE_PIN is the oldest ae this repository is
# verified against, bumped only in the commit that needs something newer.
#
# 0.875.0: the release current when the repository was set up (2026-11-04),
# and the one its tests were first run on (macOS arm64, Linux x86_64). Older
# releases were not tried. The bridge needs a release whose tarball ships
# include/aether/runtime (aether_sandbox.h) and, on Linux,
# lib/libaether_sandbox.so: both are in 0.875.0.
#
# Raised 0.875.0 -> 0.923.0 (2026-11-19): a real floor move for quickjs.
# contrib.quickjs from 0.915.0 (quickjs-ng 0.18) has no set_time_limit (an
# absolute per-runtime deadline, set_deadline_ns on now_ns's clock, replaced
# it) and its to_string returns (string, error) with the text in the runtime's
# scratch; quickjs/ is ported to both, so it needs 0.915.0 or later. Verified
# on 0.923.0, macOS arm64: quickjs, and lua, python, perl, ruby, tcl, racket,
# duktape, java, go and tinygo unchanged from their 0.923.0 counts.
#
# Raised 0.923.0 -> 0.931.0 (2026-11-20): a tracking-only bump, no new primitive
# needed and no source change. AE_CHILD_PIN and AE_SPAWN_PIN stay where they are:
# they exist to prove the older releases still work, not to follow AE_PIN. AEB_REF
# stays v0.340: nothing here runs aeb, and get.sh installs its release binary.
# Verified on 0.931.0, ae-x64 (Ubuntu 22.04 x86_64): tests/run.sh spec passes
# (factor, java and racket skip for want of their runtimes there). Containment rows on ae-x64 fail the same way on 0.923.0 and 0.931.0 (the child dlopen-libc refusals and README parity columns for other hosts), so nothing there moved.
#
# Raised 0.931.0 -> 0.933.0 (2026-11-21): a tracking-only bump again, no new primitive
# needed and no source change; the older pins below stay on purpose. Verified on
# 0.933.0, cachyos: tests/run.sh spec passes.
#
# Raised 0.933.0 -> 0.934.0 (2026-11-21): tracking-only again, no new primitive
# needed. Verified on 0.934.0, cachyos (rolling Linux, Landlock): tests/run.sh
# with GHL_REQUIRE_CHILD=1, every language, all passed once Python's child host
# granted its stdlib directory itself (the next commit), with no table cell
# changed by 0.934.0. Aether #3799's preload fixes (openat2, renameat2, glob,
# fts_open wrapped; a refused dlopen always leaves a dlerror()) change a table
# only where a row used to die on them: Tcl's two dlopen rows, restored below.
AE_PIN=0.934.0
# aeb is not used to build anything here yet; get.sh installs it with ae.
AEB_REF=v0.340
# The aether source ref stunt's catalogue is built from (stunt.c, stunt.h,
# stunt_main.c). Moved v0.875.0 -> v0.934.0 (2026-11-21): between the two,
# contrib/host/stunt changed in three places and no row was added, removed or
# renamed: stunt.c's dlopen-libm names NetBSD's and OpenBSD's libm, and the
# comment of the syscall-openat rows now says what the preload does (EPERM under
# a policy with no native grant, forwarded otherwise); aether_host_stunt.c and
# the README only say where the bridges live now. The older-pin jobs build it
# the same way (three files fetched, compiled with cc: no ae involved), and
# stunt's rows do not depend on the ae they run under. Release tarballs ship contrib/host/stunt without stunt.c and
# stunt_main.c, so the catalogue comes from the source at the release's tag.
AETHER_STUNT_REF=v0.934.0
# The oldest ae with std.guest (the contained child's protocol, aether #3555):
# 0.878.0, the first published release that contains it. 0.876.0 and 0.877.0
# were tagged but never published (no binary assets).
AE_CHILD_PIN=0.878.0
# The oldest ae whose sandbox preload holds every libc way of starting a
# program (aether #3580): posix_spawn, system and popen included, so Lua's
# os.execute and io.popen follow the exec and fork grants in-process, and the
# contained child's own lockdown (no grants) refuses them. Below it they
# escape the preload. 0.884.0 is the first release with #3580. Not a floor:
# tests/stunt_lib.sh expects one or the other side of it from the ae it runs.
AE_SPAWN_PIN=0.884.0
# The oldest ae quickjs/ builds on: 0.916.0 (checked 2026-11-21, ae-x64, with
# the child required: every row and the parity table pass). contrib.quickjs
# exports set_deadline_ns and returns (string, error) from to_string from
# 0.916.0, not 0.915.0 (aether v0.915.0's module.ae has no set_deadline_ns;
# v0.916.0's has it), and the bridge is ported to both. So the quickjs jobs
# that were to prove AE_CHILD_PIN and AE_SPAWN_PIN cannot build there (0.878.0
# and 0.884.0 fail to type-check quickjs/containment/host.ae); the quickjs
# child job runs on this one instead, and there is no quickjs spawn job: both
# sides of AE_SPAWN_PIN would need an ae from before 0.884.0, which cannot
# build quickjs, so quickjs/README.md's table has the one side.
AE_QUICKJS_PIN=0.916.0
# The first ae on which a refused dlopen always leaves a non-NULL dlerror()
# (aether #3799, 0.934.0). Before it, Tcl 8.6's load of a library the preload
# refuses formatted the NULL and the worker died (SIGSEGV in TclpDlopen), so
# Tcl's two dlopen-libc rows in the contained child are not run on an older ae
# (tcl/containment/lang.sh). Not a floor; tests/stunt_lib.sh expects one side
# of it or the other from the ae it runs on.
AE_DLERROR_PIN=0.934.0

# Factor needs the embed-api fork of Factor (factor/README.md, "Caveat 1"): a
# distribution's Factor has no libfactor with factor_embed_eval. CI builds this
# repository at this commit (the one the tests were first run against, the
# tip of its feat/embed-api when factor/ was set up, 2026-11-05) and caches
# the build under the commit. Not a floor: any later commit of the fork that
# keeps vm/embed_api.cpp's entry points should do; bumped only in the commit
# that needs a newer one. Moved c467127bc2 to 6b88e3b758 (2026-11-21), the
# fork's branch embed-no-monitors, one commit on top: the embedded VM starts
# with -no-monitors, which ends the hang a refused directory listing caused
# (asks/factor-refused-opendir-hangs-since-0.927.md). The boot image below is
# unchanged: the fork's base is the same upstream commit.
FACTOR_FORK_REPO=https://github.com/aether-lang-dev/factor-language
FACTOR_FORK_REF=6b88e3b75828ffb6ce253cf7f1d665c15f369de2
# The stock boot image the fork's factor.image is bootstrapped from, kept in
# this repository and checked against its SHA-256, not fetched. It was fetched
# from downloads.factorcode.org/images/master/, which moves with Factor's master:
# on 2026-11-17 upstream's alist commit (705ad2d, "assocs: adding an alist
# type") changed the image, and bootstrapping the fork at FACTOR_FORK_REF
# (based on upstream 6221b7e, 2026-10-31) from it dies with "Memory protection
# fault at address 0x28" before the image is saved. This is the boot image that
# was current when the fork's tree was built by hand (2026-11-01), and it
# bootstraps the fork at FACTOR_FORK_REF (checked 2026-11-21, cachyos). Factor's
# own licence (BSD) covers it; its source is upstream's core/ at that time.
# It moves with FACTOR_FORK_REF: a fork commit rebased on a newer upstream needs
# the image that upstream's master built, which has to be copied in then.
FACTOR_BOOT_IMAGE=ci/factor/boot.unix-x86.64.image
FACTOR_BOOT_IMAGE_SHA256=02c331490d75a90cac175b4d88b3d8ef4df88e72bbf3ffe870bfaaa48f6e9ada
